 "text": "Help Quote progress 30% Tell us about your home's rooms and structures Your home Which property type is your home? More about property types Rooms inside your home How many bedrooms are in your home? This includes granny flats or studies which can be used as a bedroom. Small bedrooms (around 6m\u00b2) Fits a single bed, a desk and a small bookshelf. 0 Medium bedrooms (around 9m\u00b2) Fits a queen bed, a desk and 2 bedside tables. 0 Large bedrooms (around 16m\u00b2) Fits a king bed, a desk, 2 bedside tables and a reading chair 0 How to estimate bedroom sizes How many bathrooms and ensuites are in your home? 0 Structures outside your home How many undercover parking spaces are there? Carport car spaces Usually with a roof and open sides. 0 Garage car spaces Enclosed, but not attached to the house. 0 How many sheds are there? Small sheds (under 16m\u00b2) Used to store things like gardening tools, bikes, and small equipment. 0 Large sheds (over 16m\u00b2) Used to store things like boats or machinery. 0 More about sheds How many of these outdoor structures are there? Verandahs Have a roof and run alongside your house. 0 Balconies and decks Balconies are attached to an upper level, and decks are ground level with no roof. 0 More about verandahs, balconies and decks More about outside structures Next Back Insurance issued by Insurance Australia Limited, ABN 11 000 016 722, AFSL 227681 trading as NRMA Insurance. Any advice provided is general advice only and does not take into account your individual objectives, financial situation or needs (\"your personal circumstances\"). Before using this advice to decide whether to purchase a product, you should consider your personal circumstances and the relevant Product Disclosure Statement. The Product Disclosure Statement (opens in new window) , Target Market Determinations (opens in new window) and Key Facts Sheet (opens in new window) are available from our website. *National Roads and Motorists' Association Limited, ABN 77 000 010 506, trading as NRMA,",
